---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { releases } from "../../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting started with ScreenRecorder"
  description="Install ScreenRecorder on Windows or Fedora and make your first local screen recording."
>
  <article class="guide wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/docs/">← All documentation</a><div
      class="eyebrow"
    >
      THE BASICS · 3 MIN READ
    </div><h1>
      Make your first<br /><span class="accent-word">recording.</span>
    </h1><p class="guide-lead">
      Choose the instructions for your platform, launch the app, and save a
      short test clip to make sure everything is working.
    </p><div class="guide-callout">
      <span>✳</span><p>
        ScreenRecorder saves recordings locally. The website and app do not
        upload your video.
      </p>
    </div><h2>Windows 10 / 11</h2><ol class="guide-list">
      <li>
        Download the <a href={releases.windows.url}>Windows x64 ZIP</a>.
      </li><li>Extract the ZIP to a folder you can access.</li><li>
        Run <code>ScreenRecorder.exe</code>.
      </li><li>
        Choose an output folder and capture quality, then start recording.
      </li><li>Stop the recording and open the saved MP4 to review it.</li>
    </ol><h2>Fedora 44 · GNOME / Wayland</h2><ol class="guide-list">
      <li>
        Open <a href={releases.fedora.url}>GitHub Releases</a> and choose the Fedora
        RPM for your architecture.
      </li><li>
        Install the RPM with DNF, for example <code
          >sudo dnf install ./fedora-screen-recorder-*.rpm</code
        >.
      </li><li>Launch Fedora Screen Recorder from the application grid.</li><li>
        Choose a screen or window in the desktop portal prompt.
      </li>
    </ol><h2>Check the basics</h2><p>
      Record a short clip with system audio or a microphone enabled if you need
      sound. The Windows build mixes both into one stereo track, so check their
      levels before recording.
    </p><a class="text-link guide-next" href="/docs/recording-settings/"
      >Next: recording settings →</a
    >
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
